<!--
  Adaptive-icon foreground: the Tafh light-wave mark.

  Geometry notes, because launcher masks are unforgiving:
  - The adaptive canvas is 108dp but only the central 66dp circle is guaranteed
    visible, so the glyph box is held to roughly 46x26dp centred on the canvas.
  - The wave runs half a period past each edge of its box; the round caps are what
    make it read as a wave rather than a squiggle at 24dp.
  - A single stroked path (not filled outlines) keeps the curve smooth at every
    density and lets the monochrome layer reuse the identical geometry.
-->
